{"book":13,"chapter":19,"rubric":"PYTHON AS A FIRST LANGUAGE / THE DATA MODEL / CHAPTER 19","slides":[{"title":"Plus is a method","sub":"Operators and special methods","short":"Plus is a method","main":"a + b is a call of type(a).__add__(a, b).","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One sign","Method call","Your class"],"captions":["Plus works differently for numbers, lists and strings, and sets have none at all","The reason: a + b is a notation for calling type(a).__add__(a, b)","Teach a class __add__ and your objects will add: vectors, money, matrices"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":50.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["1 + 2          # 3","[1] + [2]      # [1, 2]","'a' + 'b'      # 'ab'","{1} + {2}      # TypeError"],"bad":[3],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":260.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"a + b","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":30.0,"text":"type(a).__add__(a, b)","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":142.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":192.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["v1 = Vector(1, 2)","v2 = Vector(3, 4)","v1 + v2   # Vector(4, 6)"],"hl":[2],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":24.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"def __add__(self, other): …","tone":"green","size":10.0}]],"cues":[11.7,23.9]}]},{"title":"Arithmetic methods","sub":"Addition, subtraction, multiplication...","short":"Arithmetic","main":"Arithmetic returns a new object and keeps the operands.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Operators and methods","New object","Operands intact"],"captions":["Each arithmetic operator has its own method: add, subtract, multiply, divide, remainder, power","The method returns a new object: Vector(self.x + other.x, self.y + other.y)","The operands stay unchanged, as with numbers and strings, so no side effects"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"o0","x":56.0,"y":